PKG=gtar
NAME=GNU tar 1.14 - base-256 aware tar
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.14-2
CATEGORY=utility
CLASSES=none
VENDOR=amix-packages
# Authored PSTAMP -- an unset one leaks the build host into a distributed file.
PSTAMP=amix-packages-gtar-1.14-2
# Coexists with stock: stock SVR4 tar is /usr/sbin/tar (+ /etc/tar), owned by
# core, which this package does NOT touch.  Ours is /opt/amix/bin/tar and wins
# by PATH.  PKG is gtar so the catalog never shows two packages named tar.
DESC=GNU tar 1.14 beside stock SVR4 tar, which it does NOT replace (stock /usr/sbin/tar is untouched; ours wins by PATH). Reads base-256 headers from modern tars, long names, -z via gzip on PATH (install gzip). Owner names are looked up by its own /etc/passwd and /etc/group parsers, not the stock libc (D3). Installs /opt/amix/bin/tar; add /opt/amix/bin to PATH.
